# oracle: ReaxFF water (55 molecules cut from examples/reaxff/water data.water, 10 NVE steps) with fix acks2/reaxff (ACKS2 force field acks2_ff.water, keyword reaxff, tolerance 1e-6 as the example), b332f28 GPL-2.0
# oracle-inputs: w65reaxq_water.data w65reaxq_acks2_ff.water w65reaxq_qeq_ff.water w65reaxq_gauss_exp.txt
# Measured (engine vs native, max relative error over the 11 rows): pe 1.7e-6, ecoul 1.2e-5, ke 1.5e-6, press 2.8e-3.
# The BiCGStab iteration counts of the two codes separate after step 1 (native 59 66.5 63 56 36.5, engine 60 63 62 57 30,
# matvec halves): rounding order inside the iterative solve, so this case is compared at rel=3e-3.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=3e-3 abs=1e-8
units           real
atom_style      charge
boundary        p p p
read_data       w65reaxq_water.data
pair_style      reaxff NULL safezone 3.0 mincap 150
pair_coeff      * * w65reaxq_acks2_ff.water O H
fix             1 all acks2/reaxff 1 0.0 10.0 1.0e-6 reaxff maxiter 1000
neighbor        0.5 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
velocity        all create 300.0 4928459 rot yes dist gaussian
timestep        0.5
fix             2 all nve
thermo_style    custom step temp pe ebond evdwl ecoul ke etotal press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          1
run             10
